Gimli the dorf, entered a man, exited a woman (or goddess).  I've
ascended once before, as a tourist, and otherwise have a long top 100
list of "quit in Gehennom"s.  But for once I decided to muddle through
it all just for the hell of it, and to see if I could indeed make it
again instead of just quiting before running through maze after maze. 
I found it wasn't that difficult, but then, I used 8 wishes (none for
artifacts) and genocided 10 species (L, P, R classes).  I wish I had
taken up some challenges, just to make it more difficult; but when I
started out, I hadn't any designs to go all the way.  As ever, I was
just screwing around.

Anyway, Gimli the post-op archaeologist ascended as/with:

Level 27, 4,798,870 points, 448,600 in zorkmids plus 2gp, in 68,751
turns
STR 18/** DEX 24 CON 18 INT 20 WIS 20 CHA 14 HP 371(475) POW 78(130)
AC -40

All the common intrinsics/resists, plus teleport and regeneration
(thanks to some metallic rings); almost every spell known.

Main equipment, a typical polypile/wish-assisted kit (all
weapons/armor foo-proofed and blessed, except for a couple that were
nailed by malignant auras near the end):

+6 Grayswandir, +6 silver saber
fun daggers: 3 +7 and 2 +6 regular, 3 +7 elven, 1 +7 silver

+5 speed boots, +5 gaunts of dex, +5 cloak of displacement, +5 gdsm,
+4 helm of brilliance, +4 hawaiian shirt

rings mostly used: conflict, slow digestion, free action (my favorite
ring in the game, it seems), levitation, teleport control

5 life-saving amulets (never wore any), amulet of reflection

bagful of usual unused wands, plus a wand of death I once used on a
named demon (I forget which) and surprisingly, it worked!

blessed Orb of Detection (1:5) made the elemental levels so easy. It
didn't hurt too that Fire's exit was only about 20 steps away.  The
one which took me longest, actually, was Earth, oddly enough.

blessed bag of holding, unihorn, etc.

unused scrolls included genocides, and remove curses which I thought
I'd need but didn't

236 gems and a luckstone

important kills: Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Orcus, Yeenoghu, Jubilex, 9
Rodneys, Death, Croesus, Medusa, Vlad the Impaler, and 4 kittens. 
Plus 3092 other critters.

And after all that, I was still wishing I was playing a timid level 1
character instead of zipping through all the end levels.  I just love
the early game that much.

I wish I could remember more about this dorf's adventures, but I
wasn't keeping a more entertaining ascension post in mind.  Doh!

